window.THESIS = [
  { n:"The gods were visitors",
    t:`Every old culture says the same thing in its own words. Beings came down from the sky. They were powerful, they were not us, and they taught. The Watchers taught metalwork. The apkallu taught building and law. Viracocha and Quetzalcoatl taught farming and the calendar. I think early people described what they saw in the only language they had, and the word they had was "god".`,
    f:`Enoch, the Sumerian sage lists and the Andean and Mesoamerican teacher-gods are real texts and traditions, and they do share this structure.`,
    x:`Humans everywhere look up, and everywhere put power in the sky. Shared stories can come from shared minds.` },
  { n:"One blueprint on separate continents",
    t:`Egypt, Mesopotamia, Mexico, Peru and China had no contact with one another, and they arrived at pyramids, sky-aligned temples, flood stories and serpent teachers. I read that as one source reaching several students.`,
    f:`The monuments are aligned to the sky with real precision, and the flood and sky-teacher motifs do recur worldwide.`,
    x:`The pyramids are 2,000 to 4,000 years apart, were built by different methods, and served different purposes. A pyramid is also the only stable way to stack stone high without arches or steel.` },
  { n:"We are a hybrid",
    t:`No other species on this planet is remotely like us. The brain tripled in size in a short stretch of evolutionary time, and with it came language, art and mathematics. I think the simplest explanation for that gap is intervention: a breeding or engineering programme that crossed a local primate with something else. Genesis 6 and Enoch describe exactly that.`,
    f:`Human evolution did include hybridisation, with Neanderthals and Denisovans, and some regions of our genome changed unusually fast.`,
    x:`So far every human gene has a relative in other primates. The fused chromosome 2 that is often cited still carries the ape telomeres in its middle, which points to descent.` },
  { n:"They are zookeepers",
    t:`This is the zoo hypothesis with the keepers left in. They look after us the way we look after a reserve. They keep contact indirect and step in at hinge points: farming and building when we needed to survive the elements, and nuclear weapons when we became able to end ourselves. Their interest in missile fields is the strongest pattern in the whole record.`,
    f:`The nuclear link runs from the 1948 green fireballs through Malmstrom and Rendlesham to the pre-Sputnik plate studies of 2025.`,
    x:`Nuclear sites are also the most heavily watched places on Earth, staffed by people trained to report anything odd. And nothing stopped Hiroshima, Chernobyl or two thousand test detonations.` },
  { n:"They wear the mask of the age",
    t:`Angels and demons to a medieval farmer. Airship pilots in 1897. Space Brothers in the atomic fifties. Grey technicians in the age of medicine and machines. I think they present in whatever form a culture can absorb, which is why the descriptions keep changing while the behaviour stays the same.`,
    f:`This is Jacques Vallée's central finding, and the historical record supports the pattern.`,
    x:`The psychosocial school reads the same pattern the other way. If the form always matches the culture, the culture may be the author.` },
  { n:"The biggest secret, and what it costs",
    t:`If any of this is true it is the most valuable secret any government has ever held, and the technology behind it is the real prize. I think a small group inside the national security state has kept it for eighty years in order to reverse engineer it, outside the reach of Congress and of presidents. Carter promised to open the files and did not. Clinton sent an aide to find out and got nowhere. And I think Kennedy, who was pressing the CIA and reaching out to the Soviets on space in the weeks before Dallas, was killed for getting too close.`,
    f:`The Robertson Panel, the Bennewitz deception and decades of false cover stories are documented. Kennedy did sign an order on space cooperation with Moscow ten days before he died, and the CIA did withhold what it knew about Oswald.`,
    x:`The memo in which Kennedy supposedly demands UFO files has never been authenticated. Millions of pages of released assassination records contain no UFO link. This is the part of my theory with the least evidence behind it.` },
  { n:"We have been told already",
    t:`I do not think disclosure starts with a press conference. It has been dripping into us through fiction for seventy years, so that when the facts arrive they feel familiar. Follow Spielberg alone: contact, the hunted visitor, the hybrid child, the ancient teachers, and in 2026 a film titled after the event itself.`,
    f:`Spielberg did build Close Encounters on Hynek and Vallée. The CIA's 1953 panel did recommend using film and television to shape public feeling about UFOs.`,
    x:`That panel wanted the media to make people care less. Storytellers borrow from UFO lore and UFO lore borrows back, and that loop needs nobody directing it.` },
  { n:"The genome will settle it",
    t:`Here is my prediction, and it can fail. Within a few years AI models trained on every sequenced genome will be able to say whether human DNA carries a signature that descent cannot explain: inserted sequences with no ancestor, edits too clean to be chance. If it is there, the evidence will be public, checkable by anyone, and impossible to classify. Disclosure then stops being a decision governments get to make.`,
    f:`This is a real test. The same methods already detect Neanderthal ancestry and laboratory edits.`,
    x:`It can come back negative. If it does, the hybrid part of this theory is finished, and I would want to know that too.` }
];

